      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "There you say it, \"non-VR players\". It is called VRChat because it is not made for desktop use in the first place. You want the full experience? Get VR. Just my opinion. Or go and play Garrys Mod for example. To be honest I do not really care if desktop users can use all the stuff and do all the things. There is only one way to improve their experience and that is to get a proper HMD and some hand tracking. Mouse and keyboard or even a controller will always be the equivalent of a wheelchair in VR.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-10T04:25:51.562Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be nice if we could create custom scripts with KeyEvent handling so we can bind keys to model-specific actions like:\n\n- Animations play on keybind.\n- IK movement on keybind.\n- Custom text input that can be processed to display speech bubbles for those who do not use a mic.\n\nThese will give non-VR players more ways to interact.\n\nAlternatively some of the above can be added as a general update to improve keyboard support, but there are cases where custom key events can make models very interesting and expand creativity, like toggling mesh objects, blendshapes and IK enablers.",
